    "title": "SGA: Working Translation, Source-Repair, and Audit Drafts (SGA6 idx379 Source-Rescribe Checkpoint)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21302915",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-11",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing SGA working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. It retains the compact SGA5 and SGA6 reader-first surface and updates the front SGA6 French source-rescribe workpass to the frozen checkpoint through certification-ledger entry #376, scan idx379 / volume p366 / Expose VI p2.</p><p><strong>Open first:</strong> the SGA5 French workpass PDF, <code>01_SGA6_French_SourceRescribe_Workpass_NotCertified_idx379_20260711.pdf</code>, and the SGA6 English unsynchronized working-draft PDF. File <code>04_SGA6_TeX_SourceRescribe_Audit_NotCertified_idx379_20260711.zip</code> contains the editable French TeX, full certification and errata ledgers, compile logs, retained representative source crops, and a status README.</p><p><strong>What changed:</strong> since the idx355 public checkpoint, twenty-four page-local source passes traverse Expose V pp47-68 and enter Expose VI through p2. This delta restores two whole source pages omitted by the inherited scaffold, corrects relations and notation, repairs diagrams, and checks equation tags individually against the scan. The source-rescribe cursor passing the Expose V bibliography is a branch-workflow statement, not whole-volume or multilingual completion.</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> this is useful source-aware working material, not OCR-only, but it is not a critical edition, completed SGA6 release, whole-volume source-faithfulness certification, English synchronization, index audit, or publication-grade proofreading. Material after the stated cursor in the compiled PDF remains inherited working scaffold until directly compared with the source. SGA5 remains incomplete and SGA7 remains partial and caveat-heavy.</p><p>Corrections can be proposed through the GitHub mirror: <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
